--- answer ---
The bug is at more_itertools/more.py:2654 — after yielding the cached pred-matching items, the cache is never cleared, so those items are yielded again on the next non-matching item.Adding a regression test for the interspersed case:Test execution is denied by the sandbox policy, so I can't run the tests to verify — the fix itself is straightforward and matches the `cache_clear` setup already present in the function.

**Summary:**
- **Cause:** `rstrip` (more_itertools/more.py:2650) buffers trailing pred-matching items and yields them when a non-matching item arrives, but never cleared the cache — so cached items were re-yielded for every subsequent non-matching item, producing duplicates whenever pred-matching items appeared between non-matching ones.
- **Fix:** added `cache_clear()` after `yield from cache` (more_itertools/more.py:2655).
- Added regression test `test_rstrip_interspersed` in tests/test_more.py. I attempted to run tests and the project's compile check, but the sandbox denied all commands this turn — changes are unverified by execution.